  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nAn uneventful weather pattern will remain in place through next week \nas we sit on the periphery of ridging across the central CONUS and a \nclosed 500 mb low off to our east in an omega blocking pattern. \nSurface high pressure settles in through the weekend bringing high \nconfidence dry weather and seasonable temperatures with 70s for \nhighs and 50s for lows. Series of mid-level waves will swing through \nthe Eastern Seaboard through next week bringing very low chances of \nrain tied to uncertain shortwave timing, but even high end QPF \npotential at this point is minimal at best with scarce moisture in \ncolumn-uniform northerly component flow.\n\nEnsembles means look to regress back to more zonal flow with erosion \nof the blocking pattern by late next week perhaps allowing for some \nreturn of moisture, but the CPC's 8-14 day outlook suggests above-\nnormal temperatures and a lean below normal on precipitation for \nearly June.",
